{"5406260":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Moonlit Cat Diner","steam_appid":5406260,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"A rainy night, a little late-night diner at the end of the alley. You're the one behind the counter.<br><br>One by one, cat customers come in out of the rain and take a seat. They order, and while the game plays out, they start to talk. The more cards find their place, the more they open up — and the last part of each story only comes if you win.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Three trays<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Six solitaire games<\/strong> — Klondike, FreeCell, TriPeaks, Yukon, Pyramid and Spider, on a 90-level track that starts gentle and slowly deepens.<br><\/li><li><strong>Shisen-Sho<\/strong> — connect matching dish tiles with a path of no more than two turns. 150 boards, with shapes and stacked layers that keep changing.<br><\/li><li><strong>Six puzzle rules<\/strong> — triple match, drink sorting, merge, blocks, path linking and seating, rotating every five levels across 150 levels.<\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Twenty-six guests, one cat codex<\/h2>Every guest is a cat: a regular of fifteen years, a kitten waiting for someone, a wanderer who stepped out of a far-away legend. Codex entries aren't unlocked by winning — they fill in only when <strong>the cat tells you themselves<\/strong>. Where they're from, what they love, and the worry they find hardest to say out loud.<br><br>Regulars don't repeat themselves from the top. They notice the season, remember what they ordered last time, and spot what's new in the diner.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Make the diner yours<\/h2>Spend the coins you earn on furniture, lights, ornaments, the view outside the window, and the owner's outfit. Drag across the wide room and place things wherever you like.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >And also<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Today's Challenge<\/strong> — the same board for everyone, a new one each day<br><\/li><li>Daily quests, nights that change with weather and season, and special named nights<br><\/li><li>No hearts, no energy, no waiting. Play as long as you like<br><\/li><li>Mouse, keyboard and gamepad support<br><\/li><li>English · 한국어 · 日本語 · 简体中文 · 繁體中文 · Русский<\/li><\/ul>","about_the_game":"A rainy night, a little late-night diner at the end of the alley. You're the one behind the counter.<br><br>One by one, cat customers come in out of the rain and take a seat. They order, and while the game plays out, they start to talk. The more cards find their place, the more they open up — and the last part of each story only comes if you win.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Three trays<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Six solitaire games<\/strong> — Klondike, FreeCell, TriPeaks, Yukon, Pyramid and Spider, on a 90-level track that starts gentle and slowly deepens.<br><\/li><li><strong>Shisen-Sho<\/strong> — connect matching dish tiles with a path of no more than two turns. 150 boards, with shapes and stacked layers that keep changing.<br><\/li><li><strong>Six puzzle rules<\/strong> — triple match, drink sorting, merge, blocks, path linking and seating, rotating every five levels across 150 levels.<\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Twenty-six guests, one cat codex<\/h2>Every guest is a cat: a regular of fifteen years, a kitten waiting for someone, a wanderer who stepped out of a far-away legend. Codex entries aren't unlocked by winning — they fill in only when <strong>the cat tells you themselves<\/strong>. Where they're from, what they love, and the worry they find hardest to say out loud.<br><br>Regulars don't repeat themselves from the top. They notice the season, remember what they ordered last time, and spot what's new in the diner.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Make the diner yours<\/h2>Spend the coins you earn on furniture, lights, ornaments, the view outside the window, and the owner's outfit. Drag across the wide room and place things wherever you like.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >And also<\/h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Today's Challenge<\/strong> — the same board for everyone, a new one each day<br><\/li><li>Daily quests, nights that change with weather and season, and special named nights<br><\/li><li>No hearts, no energy, no waiting. Play as long as you like<br><\/li><li>Mouse, keyboard and gamepad support<br><\/li><li>English · 한국어 · 日本語 · 简体中文 · 繁體中文 · Русский<\/li><\/ul>","short_description":"A rainy night, a little diner at the end of the alley. Cat customers take a seat, place an order, and open up as you play — six solitaire games, Shisen-Sho, and six puzzle rules. Every story you hear fills your cat codex, and every coin you earn goes into your own diner.","supported_languages":"English, Japanese, Korean, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5406260\/4202517b7af95f1eed1e20464b846ff7bbc65e92\/header.jpg?t=1793684697","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5406260\/d29a2fa13fff17b78332591a7ae3a1a98808e436\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793684697","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5406260\/d29a2fa13fff17b78332591a7ae3a1a98808e436\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793684697","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Dual-core 2.0 GHz<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 4 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> Integrated graphics, 1280x720<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 500 MB available space<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> <br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> <br><\/li><li><str